    <title>Assignment 1 - Command Line &amp; Documentation</title>
    <link href="/2026/04/10/assignment1.md/"/>
    <url>/2026/04/10/assignment1.md/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="Remote-Development-Project-Report"><a href="#Remote-Development-Project-Report" class="headerlink" title="Remote Development Project Report"></a>Remote Development Project Report</h1><p><strong>Student Name</strong>: Qi Yongpeng<br><strong>Student ID</strong>: ZY2557206  </p><hr><h2 id="Assignment-Files"><a href="#Assignment-Files" class="headerlink" title="Assignment Files"></a>Assignment Files</h2><ul><li><p>Markdown: <a href="/files/assignment1.md">assignment1.md</a></p></li><li><p>PDF: <a href="/files/assignment1.pdf">assignment1.pdf</a></p><h1 id="System-Configuration"><a href="#System-Configuration" class="headerlink" title="System Configuration"></a>System Configuration</h1></li></ul><p>The development and testing of this project were conducted on a Linux-based environment.<br>The system configuration is summarized in the table below.</p><div class="table-container"><table><thead><tr><th>Item</th><th>Configuration</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CPU Model</td><td>Intel(R) Core(TM) i7-11800H</td></tr><tr><td>Memory Size</td><td>16GB</td></tr><tr><td>Operating System Version</td><td>Ubuntu 22.04 LTS</td></tr><tr><td>Compiler Version</td><td>GCC 11.4.0</td></tr><tr><td>Python Version</td><td>Python 3.10</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The following command line tools were used to obtain system information:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs bash">lscpu<br>free -h<br><span class="hljs-built_in">uname</span> -a<br>gcc --version<br>python --version<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>These commands allow users to inspect hardware specifications and software environment details directly from the Linux terminal.</p><hr><h1 id="Implementation-Details"><a href="#Implementation-Details" class="headerlink" title="Implementation Details"></a>Implementation Details</h1><p>Matrix multiplication is an important operation in linear algebra and is widely used in scientific computing, machine learning, and data analysis.</p><p>Given two matrices:</p><ul><li>Matrix <strong>A</strong> with dimension <strong>m × n</strong></li><li>Matrix <strong>B</strong> with dimension <strong>n × p</strong></li></ul><p>The resulting matrix <strong>C</strong> will have dimension <strong>m × p</strong>.</p><p>Each element of matrix <strong>C</strong> is calculated as:</p><figure class="highlight inform7"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs inform7">C<span class="hljs-comment">[i]</span><span class="hljs-comment">[j]</span> = sum(A<span class="hljs-comment">[i]</span><span class="hljs-comment">[k]</span> * B<span class="hljs-comment">[k]</span><span class="hljs-comment">[j]</span>)<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>This formula means that the element in row <em>i</em> and column <em>j</em> of the result matrix is obtained by multiplying corresponding elements of row <em>i</em> in matrix A and column <em>j</em> in matrix B, then summing the results.</p><hr><h1 id="Python-Language-Implementation"><a href="#Python-Language-Implementation" class="headerlink" title="Python Language Implementation"></a>Python Language Implementation</h1><h2 id="Source-Code"><a href="#Source-Code" class="headerlink" title="Source Code"></a>Source Code</h2><p>The matrix multiplication algorithm was implemented using Python.<br>The program performs multiplication using three nested loops.</p><figure class="highlight python"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br><span class="line">5</span><br><span class="line">6</span><br><span class="line">7</span><br><span class="line">8</span><br><span class="line">9</span><br><span class="line">10</span><br><span class="line">11</span><br><span class="line">12</span><br><span class="line">13</span><br><span class="line">14</span><br><span class="line">15</span><br><span class="line">16</span><br><span class="line">17</span><br><span class="line">18</span><br><span class="line">19</span><br><span class="line">20</span><br><span class="line">21</span><br><span class="line">22</span><br><span class="line">23</span><br><span class="line">24</span><br><span class="line">25</span><br><span class="line">26</span><br><span class="line">27</span><br><span class="line">28</span><br><span class="line">29</span><br><span class="line">30</span><br><span class="line">31</span><br><span class="line">32</span><br><span class="line">33</span><br><span class="line">34</span><br><span class="line">35</span><br><span class="line">36</span><br><span class="line">37</span><br><span class="line">38</span><br><span class="line">39</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs python"><span class="hljs-comment"># matrix_multiplication.py</span><br><br><span class="hljs-keyword">def</span> <span class="hljs-title function_">matrix_multiply</span>(<span class="hljs-params">A, B</span>):<br><br>    rows_A = <span class="hljs-built_in">len</span>(A)<br>    cols_A = <span class="hljs-built_in">len</span>(A[<span class="hljs-number">0</span>])<br>    cols_B = <span class="hljs-built_in">len</span>(B[<span class="hljs-number">0</span>])<br><br>    <span class="hljs-comment"># initialize result matrix</span><br>    result = [[<span class="hljs-number">0</span> <span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> _ <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">range</span>(cols_B)] <span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> _ <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">range</span>(rows_A)]<br><br>    <span class="hljs-comment"># matrix multiplication</span><br>    <span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> i <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">range</span>(rows_A):<br>        <span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> j <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">range</span>(cols_B):<br>            <span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> k <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> <span class="hljs-built_in">range</span>(cols_A):<br>                result[i][j] += A[i][k] * B[k][j]<br><br>    <span class="hljs-keyword">return</span> result<br><br><br><span class="hljs-comment"># example matrices (3x3 example)</span><br><br>A = [<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">2</span>, <span class="hljs-number">1</span>, <span class="hljs-number">3</span>],<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">0</span>, <span class="hljs-number">4</span>, <span class="hljs-number">5</span>],<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">7</span>, <span class="hljs-number">2</span>, <span class="hljs-number">6</span>]<br>]<br><br>B = [<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">1</span>, <span class="hljs-number">3</span>, <span class="hljs-number">2</span>],<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">4</span>, <span class="hljs-number">0</span>, <span class="hljs-number">1</span>],<br>    [<span class="hljs-number">5</span>, <span class="hljs-number">2</span>, <span class="hljs-number">3</span>]<br>]<br><br>C = matrix_multiply(A, B)<br><br><span class="hljs-built_in">print</span>(<span class="hljs-string">&quot;Result Matrix:&quot;</span>)<br><span class="hljs-keyword">for</span> row <span class="hljs-keyword">in</span> C:<br>    <span class="hljs-built_in">print</span>(row)<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><hr><h2 id="Execution-Command"><a href="#Execution-Command" class="headerlink" title="Execution Command"></a>Execution Command</h2><p>The program can be executed using the following command in the terminal:</p><figure class="highlight bash"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs bash">python matrix_multiplication.py<br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Expected output:</p><figure class="highlight accesslog"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br><span class="line">4</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs accesslog">Result Matrix:<br><span class="hljs-string">[21, 12, 14]</span><br><span class="hljs-string">[41, 10, 19]</span><br><span class="hljs-string">[45, 33, 34]</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><hr><h1 id="Algorithm-Verification"><a href="#Algorithm-Verification" class="headerlink" title="Algorithm Verification"></a>Algorithm Verification</h1><p>To verify the correctness of the implementation, a larger 3×3 matrix example was used.</p><p>Matrix A:</p><figure class="highlight basic"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs basic"><span class="hljs-symbol">2 </span><span class="hljs-number">1</span> <span class="hljs-number">3</span><br><span class="hljs-symbol">0 </span><span class="hljs-number">4</span> <span class="hljs-number">5</span><br><span class="hljs-symbol">7 </span><span class="hljs-number">2</span> <span class="hljs-number">6</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Matrix B:</p><figure class="highlight basic"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs basic"><span class="hljs-symbol">1 </span><span class="hljs-number">3</span> <span class="hljs-number">2</span><br><span class="hljs-symbol">4 </span><span class="hljs-number">0</span> <span class="hljs-number">1</span><br><span class="hljs-symbol">5 </span><span class="hljs-number">2</span> <span class="hljs-number">3</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Manual calculation for the first row:</p><figure class="highlight apache"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs apache"><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">1</span>][<span class="hljs-number">1</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">1</span>×<span class="hljs-number">4</span> + <span class="hljs-number">3</span>×<span class="hljs-number">5</span> = <span class="hljs-number">21</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">1</span>][<span class="hljs-number">2</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> + <span class="hljs-number">1</span>×<span class="hljs-number">0</span> + <span class="hljs-number">3</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> = <span class="hljs-number">12</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">1</span>][<span class="hljs-number">3</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> + <span class="hljs-number">1</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">3</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> = <span class="hljs-number">14</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Second row:</p><figure class="highlight apache"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs apache"><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">2</span>][<span class="hljs-number">1</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">0</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">4</span>×<span class="hljs-number">4</span> + <span class="hljs-number">5</span>×<span class="hljs-number">5</span> = <span class="hljs-number">41</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">2</span>][<span class="hljs-number">2</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">0</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> + <span class="hljs-number">4</span>×<span class="hljs-number">0</span> + <span class="hljs-number">5</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> = <span class="hljs-number">10</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">2</span>][<span class="hljs-number">3</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">0</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> + <span class="hljs-number">4</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">5</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> = <span class="hljs-number">19</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>Third row:</p><figure class="highlight apache"><table><tr><td class="gutter"><pre><span class="line">1</span><br><span class="line">2</span><br><span class="line">3</span><br></pre></td><td class="code"><pre><code class="hljs apache"><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">3</span>][<span class="hljs-number">1</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">7</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">4</span> + <span class="hljs-number">6</span>×<span class="hljs-number">5</span> = <span class="hljs-number">45</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">3</span>][<span class="hljs-number">2</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">7</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> + <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">0</span> + <span class="hljs-number">6</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> = <span class="hljs-number">33</span><br><span class="hljs-attribute">C</span>[<span class="hljs-number">3</span>][<span class="hljs-number">3</span>] = <span class="hljs-number">7</span>×<span class="hljs-number">2</span> + <span class="hljs-number">2</span>×<span class="hljs-number">1</span> + <span class="hljs-number">6</span>×<span class="hljs-number">3</span> = <span class="hljs-number">34</span><br></code></pre></td></tr></table></figure><p>The calculated results match the output generated by the Python program, confirming the correctness of the matrix multiplication algorithm.</p><hr><h1 id="Conclusion"><a href="#Conclusion" class="headerlink" title="Conclusion"></a>Conclusion</h1><p>In this project, several important concepts in software development and system operation were explored.</p><p>First, the Unix/Linux command line was used to inspect system configurations and execute programs efficiently.<br>Second, Markdown was used to create structured technical documentation that can be easily converted into other formats such as PDF.<br>Third, a matrix multiplication algorithm was implemented using Python and verified with test cases.</p><p>Through this assignment, I gained practical experience with command line tools, documentation practices, and algorithm implementation using an interpreted programming language.</p><hr><h1 id="References"><a href="#References" class="headerlink" title="References"></a>References</h1><ol><li><p>Python Official Documentation<br><a href="https://docs.python.org/">https://docs.python.org/</a></p></li><li><p>Markdown Guide<br><a href="https://www.markdownguide.org/">https://www.markdownguide.org/</a></p></li><li><p>Linux Command Line Documentation<br><a href="https://linuxcommand.org/">https://linuxcommand.org/</a></p></li></ol><hr><h1 id="Appendix"><a href="#Appendix" class="headerlink" title="Appendix"></a>Appendix</h1><h2 id="Additional-Notes"><a href="#Additional-Notes" class="headerlink" title="Additional Notes"></a>Additional Notes</h2><p>Matrix multiplication is a computationally intensive operation for large matrices.<br>Future work could involve implementing the algorithm using a compiled language such as C or C++ and comparing the execution performance between interpreted and compiled languages.</p>]]></content>
    
    
