    <title>Assignment 2 - Static Personal Blog Website</title>
    <link href="/2026/04/10/assignment2.md/"/>
    <url>/2026/04/10/assignment2.md/</url>
    
    <content type="html"><![CDATA[<h1 id="Assignment-2-Report"><a href="#Assignment-2-Report" class="headerlink" title="Assignment 2 Report"></a>Assignment 2 Report</h1><h2 id="1-Website-Setup"><a href="#1-Website-Setup" class="headerlink" title="1 Website Setup"></a>1 Website Setup</h2><p>This project builds a static personal blog using Hexo.</p><p>Steps:</p><p>1 Install Node.js<br>2 Install Hexo<br>3 Initialize blog project<br>4 Create blog posts<br>5 Deploy website</p><h2 id="2-Git-Version-Control"><a href="#2-Git-Version-Control" class="headerlink" title="2 Git Version Control"></a>2 Git Version Control</h2><p>Git is used to manage the project.</p><p>Commit history:</p><p>1 Initialize blog project<br>2 Add theme configuration<br>3 Add Assignment1 report<br>4 Add downloadable files<br>5 Deploy website</p><h2 id="3-Integration-of-Assignment1"><a href="#3-Integration-of-Assignment1" class="headerlink" title="3 Integration of Assignment1"></a>3 Integration of Assignment1</h2><p>Assignment1 report is integrated into the website.</p><p>Users can download:</p><ul><li>Markdown version</li><li>PDF version</li></ul><h2 id="4-Website-Deployment"><a href="#4-Website-Deployment" class="headerlink" title="4 Website Deployment"></a>4 Website Deployment</h2><p>The website is deployed using GitHub Pages.</p><p>Visitors can access the blog through a public URL.</p><h2 id="5-Conclusion"><a href="#5-Conclusion" class="headerlink" title="5 Conclusion"></a>5 Conclusion</h2><p>This assignment demonstrates how to build and deploy a static blog website using Hexo and Git version control.</p><h2 id="Update"><a href="#Update" class="headerlink" title="Update"></a>Update</h2><p>Minor update to the documentation structure.</p><h2 id="Future-Improvements"><a href="#Future-Improvements" class="headerlink" title="Future Improvements"></a>Future Improvements</h2><p>In the future, the blog could be extended with additional features such as comment systems, interactive pages, and improved UI design.</p>]]></content>
    
    
